class:: FFTFluxPos2
summary:: Positive spectral flux convenience wrapper
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/FFTFlux2

description::
Delegates to FFTFlux2 with positive differences enabled. Uses the Euclidean norm of increases in the selected magnitude or power spectrum. This preserves FFTFlux2 conventions; it differs from the L1 novelty used within Onsets2.

The first frame returns zero while history warms up. Results hold between FFT frames. Persistent storage is allocated at construction; the FFT buffer is read without modifying its representation. Like vanilla Onsets, this exposes spectral onset evidence, but it has no peak picking. Use Onsets2 for triggers.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
An FFT chain with the declared size.
argument:: normalize
Positive divides by current-spectrum Euclidean norm.
argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 for magnitudes or 1 for squared magnitudes.
argument:: minFreq
Lower included frequency, in Hz.
argument:: maxFreq
Upper included frequency, in Hz; zero means Nyquist.
argument:: fftSize
Literal matching FFT size, a power of two from 256 through 8192.
returns::
One nonnegative control-rate evidence value.

examples::
FFTFluxPos2 computes half-wave rectified spectral flux, summing only positive bin energy increases while discarding negative decays. In this example, it gates an ambient reverb burst exclusively on attack onsets of a drum loop: the steady tail remains completely dry, while each new drum strike injects an expansive bloom of reverberation. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: plots positive flux in real time.
code::
(
Routine({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var posFlux = FFTFluxPos2.kr(chain, fftSize: 1024);
        var gate = (posFlux > 2.0).lagud(0.005, 0.12);
        var reverb = FreeVerb.ar(source * gate, 0.8, 0.85, 0.2) * 0.35;
        var sound = (source * 0.25) + reverb;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, posFlux) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Positive Spectral Flux", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 10.0);
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

